#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# jacobi_dn

#% text
# `jacobi_dn(u, m)` gives the Jacobi elliptic function `dn(u | m)`, `sqrt(1 - m*jacobi_sn(u, m)^2)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `dn` has the real period `2*K(m)`; `dn(u | 0)` is 1 and `dn(u | 1)` is `sech(u)` (DLMF 22.2, 22.5).

#% item
# Real machine numbers and balls give numerical values. `jacobi_dn` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
jacobi_dn(1.0, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.8231610016315962

#% cell
jacobi_dn(u, 0)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
jacobi_dn(0.5, 0.9)
#% output
#= 0.8979793436947593

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `dn^2 + m sn^2 = 1`:

#% cell
jacobi_dn(0.8, 0.3)^2 + 0.3*jacobi_sn(0.8, 0.3)^2
#% output
#= 1.0

#% text
# The derivative:

#% cell
d(jacobi_dn(u, m), u)
#% output
#= -m*jacobi_cn(u, m)*jacobi_sn(u, m)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `jacobi_sn`, `jacobi_cn`, `inverse_jacobi_dn`
